{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1339,
    "dDurationMs": 3991,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bicycles are one of the most efficient and\nversatile human-powered means of transportation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5330,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we have yet devised."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6330,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But perhaps even more incredible than humans\nriding bicycles is the fact that bicycles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10670,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can ride themselves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11950,
    "dDurationMs": 4109,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes, once they’re set in motion at a sufficient\nspeed, bicycles can stay upright without any"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16059,
    "dDurationMs": 1221,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "human intervention."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17280,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A common misconception is that bikes stay\nup because of conservation of angular momentum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21360,
    "dDurationMs": 3571,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "– that is, since the wheels are spinning,\nif the bike tips to one side there’ll be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24931,
    "dDurationMs": 2969,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some sort of countering force from the wheels\nthat keeps the bike upright."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27900,
    "dDurationMs": 4940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there’s an easy way to see this explanation\nis wrong: simply lock the handlebars in place"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32840,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a moving bike will fall over just as easily\nas a stationary one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36540,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Another common misconception is that bikes\nstay upright because of their forward momentum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40320,
    "dDurationMs": 4730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, if you knock a ghost-riding bicycle\nsideways, it’ll change directions and then"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45050,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "continue merrily on its way – plainly changing\nits momentum, but nevertheless staying upright."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50210,
    "dDurationMs": 4390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What we do know about how conventional bikes\nstay upright on their own is this: when a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54600,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "moving bike starts leaning to one side, it\nalso automatically steers towards that side"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59010,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a little bit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60010,
    "dDurationMs": 4209,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The result is that the wheels come back underneath\nthe center of mass, keeping the bike balanced."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64219,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And there are three main mechanisms responsible:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66679,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, because of the backwards tilt of a\nbike’s steering axis, its front wheel actually"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70939,
    "dDurationMs": 2871,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "touches the ground slightly behind that axis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73810,
    "dDurationMs": 3599,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This means that when the bike leans to the\nleft, the upward force from the ground acts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77409,
    "dDurationMs": 3890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to turn the wheel and handlebars to the left,\nhelping the bike steer its wheels back underneath"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81299,
    "dDurationMs": 1291,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "its center of mass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82590,
    "dDurationMs": 3849,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Second, the weight of a bike’s front wheel\nand handlebars is generally distributed slightly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86439,
    "dDurationMs": 3740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in front of the steering axis, so when the\nbike leans to the left, the downward pull"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90179,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of this mass also helps turn the front wheel\nto the left, the same way divining rods will"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94299,
    "dDurationMs": 2581,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "turn towards whatever direction you tilt your\nhands."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96880,
    "dDurationMs": 3650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Third, there is indeed a gyroscopic effect\nfrom the wheels, but it doesn’t keep the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100530,
    "dDurationMs": 1240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bike upright on its own."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101770,
    "dDurationMs": 4389,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead, it helps steer: as Destin and Carl\ndemonstrate excellently in this video about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106159,
    "dDurationMs": 4570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how helicopters work, trying to tilt a spinning\nobject makes the object tilt as if you pushed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110729,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it at a point 90° away from where you did\n– it seems spooky, but basically the effect"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115429,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of your torque lags behind where you push."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117689,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now imagine this happening vertically on a\nbike, and you can see that the gyroscopic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121529,
    "dDurationMs": 4010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "precession from the bike’s leftward lean\nmakes the front wheel turn to the left, again"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125539,
    "dDurationMs": 3151,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "helping steer its wheels back underneath its\ncenter of mass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128690,
    "dDurationMs": 4049,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In short, a normal bicycle is stable thanks\nto a combination of the front wheel touching"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132739,
    "dDurationMs": 3921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the ground behind a backwards-tilted steering\naxis, the center of mass of the front wheel"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136660,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and handlebars being located in front of the\nsteering axis, and the gyroscopic precession"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140620,
    "dDurationMs": 3970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the front wheel, all of which help the\nbike automatically steer its wheels back underneath"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144590,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it when it leans."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145590,
    "dDurationMs": 2479,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At least, when it’s moving forwards at the\ncorrect speed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148069,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the bike’s going too slow, it won’t\nturn quickly enough to keep from crashing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151909,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into the ground."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152909,
    "dDurationMs": 3771,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you push the same bike backwards, the\ngyro effect will reverse but the other two"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156680,
    "dDurationMs": 3679,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "effects won’t, with the result that the\nwheels are steered out from under the bike"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160359,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when it leans."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161359,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What’s more, none of these three mechanisms\nis, on its own, the secret to bike stability:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165519,
    "dDurationMs": 3950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "here’s a bicycle that has no gyroscopic\neffect and whose front wheel touches the ground"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169469,
    "dDurationMs": 3391,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in FRONT of the steering axis yet which is\nstable without a rider."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172860,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here’s a stable rear-steering bike, and\nhere’s a design for a stable bike where"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176790,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the steering axis tilts forward instead of\nback."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179340,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On the other hand, I made my own bike totally\nunstable just by adding some extra weight"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183400,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "behind the front fork."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184930,
    "dDurationMs": 3529,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are clearly a lot of different variables\nthat can be combined in various and surprising"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188459,
    "dDurationMs": 2821,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ways to make stable and unstable bicycles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191280,
    "dDurationMs": 4070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Adding a human to help with steering and balance\ncan sometimes make unstable bikes stable,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195350,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I imagine a rider would also make some\nstable bikes unstable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196350,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But amazingly, even for a riderless bike,\nscience currently doesn’t know what it IS"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199750,
    "dDurationMs": 4379,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about the special combinations of variables\nthat enables a bike to stay up on its own."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204129,
    "dDurationMs": 31271,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We just know that some combinations work,\nand others don’t."
    } ]
  } ]
}
